{comment: Verse 1}
When He [Em]rolls up His sleeves He ain't just puttin' on the ritz
Our [Am]God is an awe[D]some [Em]God
There is [Em]thunder in His footsteps and lightning in His fists
Our [Am]God is an awe[D]some [Em]God
The [C]Lord wasn't joking when He kicked 'em out of [G]Eden
It [D]wasn't for no reason that He [G]shed [D]His  [Em]blood
His [C]return is very close and so you better be belie[G]vin'
That our [Am]God is an awe[D]some [Em]God

{comment: Chorus}
Our [C]God is an [G]awesome God
He [D]reigns from [Em]heaven above
With [C]wisdom, [G]power and love
Our [Am]God is an [D]awesome [Em]God!

{comment: Verse 2}
And when the [Em]sky was starless in the void of the night
Our [Am]God is an awe[D]some [Em]God
He spoke [Em]into the darkness and created the light
Our [Am]God is an awe[D]some [Em]God
[C]Judgement and wrath He poured out on [G]Sodom
[D]Mercy and grace He [G]gave us [D]at the [Em]cross
I [C]hope that we have not too quickly for[G]gotten
That our [Am]God is an awe[D]some [Em]God
